# Commit Message Standards

## Group Commit Standard

When creating grouped commits, use this structure:

- First line: `type(scope): concise summary`
- One blank line after the subject
- Dash-prefixed bullets only
- No blank lines between bullets
- Keep subject under 100 characters
- Keep body lines at or below 250 characters

## Release Workflow

- Group commits by cohesive slice or responsibility first, not by arbitrary file count.
- Sign grouped commits with `git commit -S`.
- Verify with `git verify-commit HEAD` before pushing.
